s retrospectively it appears  that this connection is very much  wrapped up after york new city but  that's just because we know that the two  parties haven't actually met again and  we've gotten distracted by all sorts of  things like video games elections and of  course anthropomorphic ants but  krapika's final words regarding the  troop are quite revealing i hate to  leave my business with the spiders  unfinished but it's been two days  they've probably left by now and the  eyes of my brethren should come first  meaning that krapika rather reluctantly  gave up on hunting the troop on this  particular occasion prioritizing  recovery of the curtain rise and yes  there's all sorts of themes in york new  city with krapika coming to terms with  the fact that the troops are not quite  the genocidal monsters he assumed they'd  be and in reality they're a lot more  human than anyone would like to admit  considering their horrific actions and  throughout this discussion one thing  we're going to have to come to terms  with is that crolo and karapica are  actually extraordinarily similar to one  another with the first of those being  that each of them has committed great  atrocities in the name of others with  crolo everything he does is for the good  of the troop and or meteor city and with  karapika everything he's done is for the  sake of his clan both characters very  much thrust into the darkest underbelly  of the hunt hunter world out of sheer  necessity or at least a perceived  necessity and there's many many many  more where that came from but for now  york new city was an awfully long time  ago and as i love to point out every  single chance i get togashi's  motivations and ideas have changed  radically throughout the years just  because he set up something during an  arc in the year 2001 doesn't mean that  he's still necessarily on track with  that two decades later in 2021 which by  the way happy 20th birthday york new  city arc you are so much older than i  thought you were but while togashi's  scatter brained improvisation strategy  does prevail for the most part karapika  and the troop are a very rare exception  which is proved by the existence of  hunter hunter volume 0 which provides  the events of the kurta clan massacre  but there is also a fun interview with  togashi within this volume where he is  asked why he made it in the first place  with that answer being i want to draw  the relationship slash conflict between  the phantom troop and karapika starting  from their origins i thought i would be  able to finish it quickly and i was able  to finish karapik as quickly but shortly  after a lot happened and i ended up  having to shelve it which is a  fascinating yet cryptic message what  togashi makes absolutely clear is that  he never lost sight of the krapika  phantom true plotline particularly since  volume 0 came out 12 years after york  new city ended and rather  uncharacteristically all of this time  later togashi was still hell-bent on  telling a particular story and he admits  that quote a lot happened referring to  greed island chimera ants chairman  elections and the most recently at that  time commenced dark continent r which is  important because that timing is  everything the release of this volume  telling the story if krapika's past  happened at the exact moment that both  karapika and the phantom troop became  focal points of the dark continent  events and given that togashi said he  had shelved their story following  yorknew this seems like a pretty  convenient time to dust that story off  which we do have evidence of courtesy of  mr mizeistom in chapter 381 after  discovering illumi and color to aboard  the blackwell one mizei storm  immediately craps his mental pantaloons  at the very thought of krapika learning  of the troops presence thus potentially  setting up a thread between the two  factions going forward which is a very  natural path to collision they're on  very different missions right now the  crawler's ultimate goal here is to rob  the khakian royal family a family that  krapika is currently contracted to  protect or at least protect one of them  the small one so all going well for the  phantom troop they will encounter  karapaka at some point however that very  much depends on your definition of the  word well because in that very same  interview in volume zero togashi quite  literally stated the ultimate fates of  both krapika and the troop which is they  will all die and i have said this before  but it's really hard to judge the  context of this statement it may very  well be a joke that doesn't translate  well between languages and especially on  paper but it could certainly be a  serious response as well in fact that's  very much what we need to take it as by  default because we have no discernible  evidence of humor how are they going to  die though well for most of the troop  it's unlikely to be cropper caused  because currently hisoka is bungle  nutting his way around the blackwell one  with the intention of hunting and  killing each and every member of the  troop furthermore they're also embroiled  in all sorts of mafia power struggles on  the lower decks and in particular they  are set up against morena and her  followers who will eventually reach an  insane quantity of power thanks to  morena's video game leveling and ability  they're in a bad spot a very bad spot  especially if they continue to be  separated the greatest strength of the  troop is being able to act as a  collective in any given situation one of  them will have the utility skill  required for a mission to succeed but  fractured they are very vulnerable  especially in a confined space filled  almost exclusively with other trained  men using killing dudes but to zero in  on kroller for a bit here is our big  twist right now he's hunting hisoka for  the crimes of murdering cortopian shanna  crollo has put his royalty robbing  mission to one side simply for the task  of delivering sweet revenge upon hisoka  revenge for your murdered loved ones  does that sound familiar to anyone else  prollo is in the exact spot that his  actions placed karapika in the troop  murdered the kurt clan and karapika  swore revenge on the spiders now members  of crollo's little clan have been  brutally murdered and he has sworn  revenge on the person clown man  responsible which actually makes it very  difficult to feel any kind of sympathy  for crawler while the phantom trooper  large because they're just experiencing  a dose of the torment that their actions  have been causing all along unless  you're takashi of course because he  actually quite admires crawler and in  fact crawler was his favorite member of  the troop allegedly because of his  selfless nature this was also revealed  in volume 0 but togashi holds a deep  distrust of elected officials as well as  leaders in general people who in his  words nominate themselves for leadership  meanwhile crolo is a man who was elected  by the founding troop members and  regardless of what his deeds are  everything he enacts is for the  betterment of the group as opposed to  his own personal benefit something that  karapika realizes in chapter 117 when he  says i assume the spiders would fall  apart once their head was removed but  that's not how they work the spiders  keep going even without their head so as  twisted as it is crolo is a selfless  antagonist and from his perspective  probably a protagonist he cares much  more for those around him than he does  for himself but we've now gotten a taste  of his darker side during the succession  war and that's just the result of two  members dying so what would happen in  the event where everyone died leaving  crollow all alone the spider head  without his spider legs well that's my  prediction i think that on this path  towards everyone dying at some stage  crollo will be the last surviving member  of the troop perfectly mirroring  karapika's situation with the kurt clan  and at this stage down the line is when  karapika will encounter crolo and he  will have a decision to make the only  trouble being that krapika may have to  continue his journey of mental growth  back in york new city he came to terms  with the fact that the troop were a  community of their own they have their  own rules practically their own society  and their own personal care for one  another not too far from the idea of a  traveling clan and as twistedly painful  as it may be grapika could be put in a  situation where he legitimately  empathizes with kroller which i imagine  would only further enrage garoppolo i  mean the thought of empathizing with the  man who ordered the slaughter of your  entire village for the sake of making a  bit of money but that's the kind of  stark confrontation that togashi handles  absolutely masterfully the best example  we currently have of such mental  conflicts would obviously be the chimera  ants a lot of that arc was very much  about questioning who the real monsters  were during this time we saw human  characters devolve into unfeeling brutal  monsters and we saw literal ant monsters  develop into highly sympathetic human  existences so a similar swap would  certainly be possible with kraftwicker  and krollo except in this case we would  just be flipping around the role of the  victim which actually provides karapika  with quite possibly his only chance for  redemption if he were to encounter  crollo recognize a cycle of revenge and  then decide to break it or at the very  least not participate in it any further  and we've been talking a lot about  krapika's feelings but crawler's  perspective is also very important here  because in the event that he meets with  karapika he will also be able to  empathize with and perhaps even take  responsibility for what he's done or at  least offer a gesture of apology before  promptly removing himself from this  world which is one of our numerous  endgame options for kroller with his  legs entirely dismembered he may just  decide to end it all because who is he  going to go on fighting for another is  that crawler lets revenge fully consume  him and his life comes to a fiery  conclusion perhaps in some kind of  hisoka-based battle and this could also  work because it would give karapika a  tangible example of his own future fate  should he continue down this path and  then give him that last minute chance to  jump out meanwhile you could also go a  bit weirder and focus on crolo's keen  reference to jesus he invert a cross on  his back the collective of twelve  disciples and so on and so forth he's  very jesus-y which holds the potential  of perhaps crawler sacrificing himself  for the sake of the troop in very much  the same way that mr jesus died on a  cross for all of all of the people which  may not play into togashi's words about  everyone dying so nicely but it doesn't  exclude the option because they can  still die and be brought back hisoka is  a prime example of that he quite  literally died and then brought himself  back from death maybe hisoka here's the  jesus but given that crolo can mix and  match every inability he comes across i  would not put it past him to conjure up  a nen resurrection spell at the cost of  his own life it does seem like a very  crowley thing to do sacrifice the head  so that the legs can live and in keeping  with religious theming perhaps even ask  forgiveness from karapika because when  it comes down to it what we have is an  eventual clash that togashi has never  lost sight of a story he feels he needs  to tell which involves two young men  geniuses or genie i what's the plural of  genius you know what i don't care two  young nen genie i both specialists as  well with a complex suite of swiss army  style and abilities both of whom are  thrust into tragedy at a young age  through no fault of their own and both  of them now doing what they feel is in  the best interest of their respective  groups and both of them set to become  the last remaining member of their clans  but i do feel that the ultimate decision  will rest with grapika this is his story  after all and for better or worse his  choice to make he can suffer revenge or  he can suffer redemption neither will be  particularly easy and in the ominous  words of yoshihiro tagashi it will very  very likely cost his life either way  probably worth it though as is this next  video because there's always more to  learn explored experience with this  wonderful series so i look forward to  seeing you there

